WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:03.620
There's a lot to look forward to at the box
office in the coming year.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.720
From superhero action thrillers to down-to-earth
dramas and everything in between, here are

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:10.740
all the movies that will blow you away in
2019.

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:16.279
M. Night Shyamalan continues his surprise
superhero trilogy with Glass, a sequel to

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:21.020
2017's Split, whose final act unexpectedly
tied in with 2000's Unbreakable.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:25.600
The movie will bring back all the main players
from both films, with Bruce Willis, Samuel

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:29.780
L. Jackson, James McAvoy, and Anya Taylor-Joy
all confirmed to return.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.480
As revealed in the first trailer, the story
also involves a psychiatrist played by Sarah

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.900
Paulson who observes the three men in an institution
while probing their "delusions of grandeur."

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:44.510
Speaking with Vulture, Shyamalan described
Glass as a story about the struggle between

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:45.840
"doubt versus belief.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:50.720
Given Shyamalan's love of twists, there's
certainly more to Glass than we know, but

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:54.560
this is a story nearly 20 years in the making,
so we're sure the director knows what he's

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:55.060
doing.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:58.340
Glass is slated to arrive in theaters on January
18th.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:04.500
Marvel's first female-led superhero film will
be long overdue when it hits theaters on March

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.220
9th, 2019, but the movie is shaping up to
be worth the wait.

00:01:08.609 --> 00:01:14.240
For one thing, Captain Marvel has Oscar winner
Brie Larson as Carol Danvers, and Marvel Studios

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:19.270
president Kevin Feige has said she'll be,
quote, "as powerful a character as we've ever

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:20.060
put in a movie."

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:25.119
The studio has directors Anna Boden and Ryan
Fleck at the helm for an origin story for

00:01:25.119 --> 00:01:29.819
Carol, all of which should help sow the seeds
for Marvel's Phase Four storylines while setting

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:34.440
up a new hero who's sure to be a key component
of the fight against Thanos in Avengers 4.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:38.640
As if that weren't enough, the film's first
trailer makes it clear that we can expect

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.440
plenty of space action and more than a few
laughs.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.480
2019 is going to be a good year for horror–and
a good year for Stephen King.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:51.680
In addition to It: Chapter 2, the year will
also see the release of Pet Sematary, based

00:01:51.689 --> 00:01:56.420
on Stephen King's 1983 novel about a family
that moves in next to a burial ground with

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.200
disturbing powers that prove too difficult
to resist.

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:04.060
The book was previously adapted for the big
screen in 1989, but the newest version of

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:08.940
Pet Sematary has some horror visionaries on
board in directors Kevin Kolsch and Dennis

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:15.060
Widmyer, who previously worked on Starry Eyes
as well as episodes of MTV's Scream TV series.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:20.690
Jason Clarke is attached to the role of Dr.
Louis Creed, first played by Dale Midkiff

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:22.200
in the 1989 Pet Sematary film.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:27.600
Joining Clarke for the remake is Amy Seimetz
as Louis' wife Rachel, and John Lithgow, who

00:02:27.611 --> 00:02:32.360
is set to portray the Creeds' neighbor Jud
Crandall, who knows all the dark secrets of

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:35.140
the animal burial site after which the movie
is titled.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:40.060
With an experienced crew and a stellar cast
locked in place, not to mention a suitably

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:44.690
freaky first trailer, Pet Sematary should
make for a spooky Easter weekend when it premieres

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:45.360
April 5th.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:50.880
Shazam! has been a long time in the making,
but the DC Comics movie is currently slated

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.900
to finally hit theaters on April 5th, 2019.

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:59.680
The movie finally found a star in October
2017 in Chuck's Zachary Levi, who will play

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.150
the grown-up superhero that teen Billy Batson
is able to turn into when he utters the magic

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:04.680
word.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:05.780
"Shazam"

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:07.820
"Are you for real?"

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:08.580
"Say it!"

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.080
"Okay...Shazam?"

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:14.120
The movie's first trailer made a splash at
Comic-Con by making it clear it'll bring a

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.720
different tone to the DC Universe.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:20.780
Its premise means it is sure to be a bit more
ridiculous and humorous than DC's past movies,

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:24.570
and the young hero should allow for the mix
of fantastical and real-life problems that

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:26.920
have served superhero films well in the past.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:30.560
While Black Adam won't appear now that he's
getting his own standalone movie, the film

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:35.680
has recruited a scary villain in Mark Strong,
who is rumored to be playing Doctor Sivana,

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:37.240
Shazam's arch-nemesis.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:41.900
"Have you ever noticed how in Hollywood movies
all the villains are played by Brits?"

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.000
"Maybe we just sound right."

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.420
The behind-the-scenes crew also hints at a
different DC film than we've seen before,

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:55.680
with Jack the Giant Slayer's Darren Lemke
attached to work on the script and Lights

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.940
Out's David F. Sandberg set to direct.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.700
"I choose you as champion."

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:10.080
David Harbour will unveil his new take on
Hellboy on April 12th, 2019, with the Stranger

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:14.700
Things star joining director Neil Marshall
for what's described as a gritty take on the

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:16.900
classic Mike Mignola comics.

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:21.720
Harbour has said the movie will use a "darker
tone" to differentiate itself from Guillermo

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:25.690
del Toro's adaptations, adding it'll be more
of "a character piece."

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:30.630
While Harbour's take on Hellboy looks spot
on, the rest of the cast is also packed with

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:36.270
potential, including Milla Jovovich as the
villainous Blood Queen, Sasha Lane as Alice

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:39.800
Monaghan, and Ian McShane as Hellboy's adopted
father.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.640
Maybe he'll teach young Hellboy a few combat
moves.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.100
"Get ready to meet your maker!

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:45.820
Ow!

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:46.680
God!

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:48.620
We hadn't even started yet!"

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.340
"Never underestimate your opponent."

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:51.060
"ARGH"

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:55.640
The fourth Avengers film will mark the end
of Marvel's Phase 3, which means it's probably

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:57.820
time to break out your tissues.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:02.640
The current set of films is coming to an end,
and many of the big-name contracts are expiring

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:03.140
as well.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.240
"I'm doing what has to be done to stave off
something worse."

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:09.660
"You keep telling yourself that."

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:15.260
In other words, Avengers 4 will probably result
in quite a few character deaths, with Iron

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:19.780
Man, Captain America, Thor, and more all likely
to bite the dust.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:24.570
With the no-holds-barred approach the studio
will likely have to the film, Avengers 4 is

00:05:24.570 --> 00:05:29.560
sure to be epic, ending dozens of storylines
set up in past films while also placing the

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:32.120
framework for what's to come in the franchise's
future.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:35.419
This is definitely one of the can't-miss adventures
of the year.

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:36.490
It arrives on May 3rd.

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:42.860
Keanu Reeves' animal-loving hitman is coming
back to theaters on May 17th, 2019 for John

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:43.760
Wick: Chapter 3.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.760
The film will see Wick going on the run with
a $14 million contract for his head.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:53.100
Having broken the rules and taken a life on
the grounds of the Continental Hotel, Wick

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:55.750
finds that he's being targeted on all sides.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:06:00.600
The crafty killer for hire should already
be long dead, but he's given a chance to escape

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:04.700
by the Continental's manager, Winston, who
grants him a one-hour grace period before

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:09.130
his membership is revoked, he's banned from
all services, and he's cut off from the other

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:09.620
members.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:13.640
Wick turns to the service industry to stay
alive as he fights his way out of New York

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:18.180
City in this third installment, which is directed
by the previous films' Chad Stahelski.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:21.500
Of course, we're pretty sure there's only
one way it can all end:

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:23.540
"I'll kill them.

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:26.400
I'll kill them all."

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:32.560
Godzilla: King of the Monsters is the follow-up
to the well-received 2014 film featuring the

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:37.730
monster and brings in a largely overhauled
roster of stars, with Stranger Things' Millie

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:43.070
Bobby Brown, The Conjuring's Vera Farmiga,
and Friday Night Lights' Kyle Chandler playing

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:45.880
a family swept up in the trouble the monster
causes.

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:50.300
With the impressive cast, Godzilla: King of
the Monsters should be able to live up to

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:54.440
the positive reviews of the original while
providing more big-screen monster mayhem.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:59.960
As the first trailer indicates, the big green
guy can expect a lot of company in this installment,

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:02.760
and it isn't necessarily of the friendly variety,
either.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.320
Look for it on May 31st.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:09.540
Tom Holland's Spider-Man is set to continue
his adventures in a second standalone film

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:14.440
on July 5th, 2019, which will follow another
year of Peter's high school experience.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:19.160
The first movie was wildly successful with
both critics and fans, and the second is bringing

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:23.500
back a lot of the elements that contributed
to its greatness, including director Jon Watts,

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:28.100
who's working from a script by Homecoming
co-writers Jonathan Goldstein and John Francis

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:28.600
Daley.

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:33.420
Despite all the returning names in the film's
crew, Spider-Man: Far From Home will be far

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:34.240
from the same movie.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:38.480
The sequel takes our friendly neighborhood
Spidey to Europe over summer vacation, which

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:43.700
happens after both Avengers: Infinity War
and Avengers 4, according to Marvel Studios

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:44.820
president Kevin Feige.

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:50.060
Hopefully that means a big return for Spidey
in Avengers 4, or he'll need some extra help

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:50.880
getting around.

00:07:51.220 --> 00:07:53.680
"I'm honestly, I'm, I'm shocked"

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:55.900
"Ahh!"

00:07:56.740 --> 00:08:00.760
Pennywise will make his terrifying return
to the big screen in September 2019.

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:06.020
It: Chapter Two is set to hit theaters almost
exactly two years after the first film, which

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:10.140
followed the lives of a group of children
known as the Losers' Club as they dealt with

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:11.980
the advances of a shapeshifting evil.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:24.960
The sequel will move to the present, showing
the adult versions of the characters as they

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:28.600
return to the town of Derry to deal with Pennywise's
reemergence.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:33.820
Director Andy Muschietti is set to return
for the sequel, alongside screenwriter Gary

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:34.320
Dauberman.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:39.460
The first film's massive box office haul and
critical acclaim meant it was easy to land

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:45.310
big name stars to play the adult Losers, with
Jessica Chastain, James McAvoy, Bill Hader,

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:48.060
Jay Ryan, and James Ransone set to appear.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:52.690
The movie's child actors will likely return
as well, with Muschietti saying there will

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:54.560
be "dialogue between timelines."

00:08:54.740 --> 00:09:00.100
Muschietti has also said he would like the
second film to explore the "cosmic dimension"

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:03.260
of the novel, dealing with some of its otherworldly
aspects.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:04.180
Sign us up.

00:09:04.680 --> 00:09:10.140
No joke: Two standalone films featuring Gotham
City's most infamous tormentor are being produced

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:13.980
in 2019, and one could even get released before
the end of the year.

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:20.260
Variety reported in June 2018 that Jared Leto's
DCEU Joker is getting his own movie, but it's

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:25.420
still unknown if it will film before or after
the upcoming Suicide Squad sequel, set to

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:27.360
go into production in 2019.

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:29.040
And then there's the wild card.

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:36.060
A Joker origin movie outside the DCEU starring
acting powerhouse Joaquin Phoenix is now under

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:36.560
way.

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:41.680
This means there's a chance this reportedly
"darker and more experimental" take on Batman's

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:46.020
iconic arch-nemesis, directed by The Hangover's
Todd Phillips, could make it into theaters

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.460
in October 2019.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:52.140
Warner Bros. describes the script, co-written
by Phillips and Academy Award nominee Scott

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:57.100
Silver as "a gritty character study, but also
a broader cautionary tale."

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:58.820
Sounds like no laughing matter.

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:04.140
There have been some shake-ups behind the
scenes of Star Wars: Episode IX, with Lucasfilm

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:08.830
dropping Jurassic World helmer Colin Trevorrow
a few months before production was set to

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:09.360
begin.

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:14.180
They found someone who's definitely qualified
to take over, however, with The Force Awakens'

00:10:14.180 --> 00:10:17.800
J.J. Abrams returning to write and direct
the trilogy finale.

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:22.740
Episode IX will provide a resolution to the
Skywalker saga while setting up a future of

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:27.730
standalone movies and spinoffs, meaning that
while we're undoubtedly in for the final appearances

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:32.640
of some classic characters, this chapter will
also serve as a launching pad for years of

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:33.900
the franchise's future.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.480
It's set to hit theaters in December 2019.

